  "status": "present",
  "value": "n = 2^h - 1 servers form a perfect binary tree (children of i are 2i+1 and 2i+2). latency[i] >= 1 is the latency added at server i; a request to a leaf costs the sum of latencies on the root-to-leaf path. Latencies may only be increased, by any integer amounts. Return the minimum total increase that makes every root-to-leaf path cost equal.",
